    "lastText": "`ledger` is built as TASK.md describes, and `npm test` passes all 13 tests.\n\nThe tests run the real CLI and cover each command. They also check the 0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30 case, monthly repeats clamping to short months, error exit codes, import with bad rows, and `undo`. I did not run commands by hand beyond that.\n\n- **Layout:** `bin/ledger.js` is the CLI entry. The library code is in `src/`, the tests in `test/`, and `README.md` has an example for every command. There are no npm dependencies.\n- **Undo:** the file keeps an undo history (up to 100 steps) alongside the transactions, so `undo` works across separate runs. Ids are never reused, even after an undo.\n- **Import:** a bad header makes `import` exit with 2. A valid file with some bad rows imports the good rows and exits 1. An import is undone as one step.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
